    fix(chat): report compaction instead of "waiting for model" during auto-compaction (#1008)
    
    * fix(chat): report compaction instead of "waiting for model" during auto-compaction
    
    Auto-compaction can hold a turn for a while before the next token arrives.
    While it runs, the chat UI reported "Waiting for model..." and offered only a
    generic Stop button, which reads as a hang and gives the user the wrong control.
    
    ## What was wrong
    
    `agentPhase` is set once when the prompt is sent (handleSend sets
    `waiting_model`) and nobody updated it when compaction began. `phaseLabel()`
    only looked at the phase, so it kept reporting the stale `waiting_model`.
    
    The compaction control was worse. It is guarded by:
    
        {!isStreaming && onCompact && ( ... )}
    
    Manual compaction starts from an idle session, so the button is already
    rendered and simply flips to "Stop compaction" when `isCompacting` turns true.
    Auto-compaction starts *mid-turn*, where `sessionBusy` is already true, so the
    button never rendered at all and only the generic Stop remained. That guard
    also contradicted the button's own `disabled={isStreaming && !isCompacting}`,
    which only makes sense if the button is meant to be reachable while streaming.
    
    Manual compaction therefore looked correct and auto-compaction did not, which
    is why this went unnoticed.
    
    ## What changed
    
    `phaseLabel()` takes `isCompacting` and returns the compaction label ahead of
    the phase, so the status names the activity that is actually blocking the turn.
    The render condition accepts a missing phase while compacting.
    
    The compaction control guard becomes `(!isStreaming || isCompacting)`, so the
    control is reachable mid-turn. Both actions stay available: "Stop compaction"
    sends `abort_compaction` and skips the compaction so the turn continues, while
    Stop sends `abort` and drops the whole turn. The now-unreachable
    "streaming but not compacting" branches (disabled, dimmed opacity, not-allowed
    cursor, the hover early-return) are removed rather than left as dead code.
    
    `phaseLabel()` moved to lib/chat-phase-label.ts so it can be unit tested;
    importing ChatWindow.tsx in a test pulls in next/image and the whole component
    tree, so it cannot be loaded in node.
    
    ## Result
    
    | | before | after |
    |---|---|---|
    | auto-compaction status | Waiting for model... | Compacting… |
    | auto-compaction control | Stop | Stop compaction (+ Stop) |
    | idle / manual | unchanged | unchanged |
    
    ## Verification
    
    - tsc: 0 errors from this change (the 2 remaining are pre-existing SDK drift)
    - lint: clean
    - tests: 1308 pass / 4 fail — the same 4 fail on upstream main
    - 5 new tests: phase label per phase, compaction precedence, and the control
      guard reaching mid-turn
    
    * fix(demo): leave the demo copies of ChatInput/ChatWindow untouched
    
    The demo resolves @/lib against demo/lib, which has no chat-phase-label
    module, so importing it there breaks the Pages build. The demo keeps its
    own copies and is synced separately (demo/README.md).
    
